when model checking....
use MTBDD engine
using "nopre" speeds up verification

==========================================================================

give two/one version(s) of the ordering of the messages
then students must come up with other 2/3 or their own
(have an additional ordering from one of the reviewers 
of the paper)

egl1:
...
party A sends bit l for secrets 1..2N
party B sends bit l for secrets 1..2N
...

egl2:
...
party A sends bit l for secrets 1..N
party B sends bit l for secrets 1..N
party A sends bit l for secrets N+1..2N
party B sends bit l for secrets N+1..2N
...

egl3:
...
party A sends bit l for secrets 1
party B sends bit l for secrets 1
...
party A sends bit l for secrets i
party B sends bit l for secrets i
party A sends bit l for secrets i+1
party B sends bit l for secrets i+1
...
party A sends bit l for secrets 2N
party B sends bit l for secrets 2N
...

egl4:
...
party A sends bit l for secrets 1
party B sends bit l for secrets 1..N
party A sends bit l for secrets 2..N
party A sends bit l for secrets N+1
party B sends bit l for secrets N+1..2N
party A sends bit l for secrets N+2..2N
...


egl5 (idea no party ahead by more than one bit):
party A sends bit l for secrets 1
party B sends bit l for secrets 1,2
party A sends bit l for secrets 2,3
party B sends bit l for secrets 3,4
...
party A sends bit l for secrets i,i+1
party B sends bit l for secrets i+1,i+2
...

The above only changes the module "scheduler". The final change concerns
changing the protocol such that if a party sends a sequence of bits in a
row then these get combined into a single message. To model this we must
change the modules of the hosts as all the bits included in the message
must get updated when the message is sent.

Note that this means that for some of the different versions of the
schedulers the modules for the different parties are no longer symmetric
(i.e. we cannot use renaming). This is true for the ordering egl4 and egl5.
Also note that egl3 does not change (neither party sends more than one bit 
in a row).

